            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is very good and goes very good with any kind of cheese to make a very good cheese sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2002-11-29T17:50:42.370Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mike O"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Use a stainless steel pan and stir with a steel spatula. This allows you to cover more surface area vs using a spoon and results in less likely to burn.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-04T14:30:48.347Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Moma Lama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "White sauce isn't sopposed to be THE flavor, it's the base. You add cheese or other ingredients to achieve the flavor you desire. \nHaving said that, this is a wonderful basic white sauce recipe. My technique and the way I teach people to make it is a bit different. \nI melt butter with salt &amp; pepper. If I'm adding onion, bell pepper etc. I do it now. When butter is melted, veggies softened I add the flour slowly whisking in in. I cook the flour mixture, stirring to cook the flour &amp; eliminate the floury taste. After about 5 minutes slowly whisk in the milk. Continue to whisk or stir it as it thickens. Then you can add grated cheese or whatever your final destination indicates. Stir, keep over low heat &amp; enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-28T23:47:21.767Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elynn Lo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super simple béchamel. I would say that you put the flour and milk together (mason jar shake works well) and then add it to melted butter; lessen chance of lumps. I added some simple seasoning and it was really good. Great base for all recipes that calls for white sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-12T03:21:07.693Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ferryal Lackey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent white sauce. Have been looking for a great white sauce for long time, however, most recipes call for cream cheese, heavy creams and or loads of cheese, it is specially hard as I am lactose intolerant. Made this with lactaid free milk and it turned out fantastic. Followed the recipe exactly and added dried basil &amp; oregano for serving over pasta. This is an absolute keeper. Thank you for sharing your recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-22T00:09:53.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
